{"_id":"68a7361e8ec3d8323af18384","nodeId":"2KyzUjcMiMgo_AvlPjYbx","roadmapSlug":"golang","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:09.800Z","description":"# panic and recover\n\n`panic()` stops execution and unwinds stack, `recover()` catches panics in deferred functions. Use sparingly for unrecoverable errors. While Go emphasizes explicit errors, panic/recover serve as safety net for exceptional situations.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Defer, Panic, and Recover","url":"https://go.dev/blog/defer-panic-and-recover","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d96e"},{"type":"article","title":"Handling Panics in Go","url":"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/handling-panics-in-go","_id":"6a26767c7e97c9d3f8b8d96f"}],"updatedAt":"2026-06-08T07:59:56.882Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/golang/content/2KyzUjcMiMgo_AvlPjYbx.md"}